--         (cLp A (cPass B E.length Bb) Bb)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFL §13: the correction, the radix sort on the stacks*: The extracted entries `E` (keys on `sKK`, records on `sKB`, entry `0` on top) are sorted by
--   `A` LSD passes.  A pass pops every entry and pushes it on the bucket of its low key bit
--   (`sZ0K/sZ0B` or `sZ1K/sZ1B`, the key halved), then moves bucket 0 and then bucket 1 back:
--   the result is `rpass i E` (`passB_fsp`).  `radix_fsp`: `A` passes give `rsort A E`.
--   All per-entry work is linear in the word size (`Sp.push`, `Sp.asg` on linear expressions).
--
